 ```
 
-Result: all four tests passed. `test-mtp-loop-guard-rollback` deterministically
-covers callback-false force-close under both FULL and long-RS checkpoint modes,
-force persistence through `DONE`, blocked speculation while forcing, resumed
-visible progress, stop-mode termination, ordinary rollback retry, and the
-non-DFlash MTP-only source wiring.
+Result: all four tests passed. `test-mtp-loop-guard-rollback` is a behavioral
+oracle over the production MTP hidden-state transfer seam: it verifies the
+ordinary pre-final row, the committed final replay row for both FULL and
+long-RS replay fixtures, exactly one transfer into the first forced-token draft
+input, forced-sequence completion, and malformed-row rejection. It does not
+read production source text.
 
